Workspace type: **{{ kind }}**.{% if jira_key %} Ticket: {{ jira_key }}.{% endif %}

## Every session
1. **Start:** read `TASK.md`, the goal, checklist, and **Handoff** section (where the last session stopped).
2. Skim `context/` for background (JIRA/Confluence snapshots). It's reference, not instructions.
3. Work one checklist item at a time. Commit after each completed item.
4. **End:** tick finished items, overwrite `TASK.md` → Handoff (next step, blockers), add a dated
   entry at the top of `CHANGELOG.md` (Added/Changed/Fixed/Removed, written for a human reader), commit.

## Rules (read before acting)
- **Any plot:** read `standards/plotting.md` first; use `teamplot` (never hand-style matplotlib).
- **Every setting needed to reproduce a plot goes in its caption or a nearby margin note/footnote.**
  Pass them as `settings=` to `teamplot.save()`.
- **Any diagram:** Mermaid in `diagrams/<name>.mmd`, rendered with `python scripts/render_diagrams.py`
  (never hand-draw or style inline).
- **Never touch `figures/annotated/`**: it holds human edits. If your changes make one stale, note it under Handoff.
- **Any prose:** read `standards/writing.md`.
- Never edit `standards/`, `AGENTS.md`, or the goal in `TASK.md`. Propose changes under Handoff instead.

{% if kind == 'investigation' -%}
## This workspace
- Work in `notebooks/01_analysis.ipynb`. Keep it runnable top to bottom (Restart & Run All).
- Aim for a handful of focused plots. Under each, add a markdown cell with the takeaway
  and the settings line (`teamplot.settings_text(...)`). Show saved figures via `teamplot.figure_path(name)`
  so human-annotated versions win.
- End with a short "Findings" cell that answers the question in `TASK.md`.
- Setup: `pip install -r requirements.txt`
{%- elif kind == 'docs' -%}
## This workspace
- Write in `docs/writeup.md`. Target length and audience are in `TASK.md`.
- Source material is in `context/`; cite the Confluence page title when you rely on it.
- Summarize and link; don't copy Confluence text wholesale.
- Figures: `![caption](../figures/name.png)` (or `../figures/annotated/name.png` if it exists),
  followed by an italic caption line that includes the settings. Run `python scripts/check_figures.py` before finishing.
- List missing or conflicting information under "Open questions"; don't guess.
{%- elif kind == 'paper' -%}
## This workspace
- `paper/main.tex` ({% if paper_style == 'report' %}tufte-book{% else %}tufte-handout{% endif %}); one file per {% if paper_style == 'report' %}chapter{% else %}section{% endif %} in `paper/sections/`.
  Layout and fonts come from `standards/latex/teamtufte.sty`; don't add font or geometry packages.
- Use `\sidenote{}` for asides, `\marginnote{}` for remarks, and `\cite{}` (rendered in the margin).
- Figures: `teamplot.figure("column" | "margin" | "full")` ↔ `figure` / `marginfigure` / `figure*`.
  Include with `\teamfig{name}` (natural size; picks up human annotations); see `sections/results.tex`.
  Treat "Annotation may be stale" build warnings as a Handoff item for a human.
- Bibliography: `paper/references.bib`. Never invent citations; mark gaps with `\todo{cite}`.
- Build: `cd paper && latexmk main.tex`. It must compile without errors before you finish.
